Toolchain of record
===================

This file pins the toolchain used to build, test, and reproduce this project.
All supporting roles are filled by the language runtime's standard library so
that the dependency surface (and therefore the lockfile scanned for prohibited
tokens) stays minimal. No external task runner, bundler, or orchestrator is used.

Runtime / language
  Node.js            24.x LTS line (developed against 24.16.0)
  TypeScript         5.7.3   (strict mode; the type checker is also the lint gate)
  ECMAScript modules, NodeNext resolution

Sole chain / cryptographic dependency
  @bsv/sdk           2.1.4   (Bitcoin (BSV) transactions, scripts, headers,
                              double-SHA256, secp256k1 group operations — the
                              BSV curve)

Supporting roles, all from the Node.js standard library (no third-party packages)
  test runner        node:test
  assertions         node:assert
  argument parser    node:util parseArgs
  HTTP server        node:http
  timing / benchmark node:perf_hooks
  structured logger  implemented in-tree over node:console (JSON lines)
  schema validator   implemented in-tree (typed validators)
  seeded RNG         implemented in-tree (deterministic)
  property testing   implemented in-tree (seeded generators)

Build
  tsc -b              project-reference build across the workspace
  npm workspaces      package linking (no third-party monorepo tool)

Reproduction hardware note
  All absolute timings reported by the studies are labelled "local" and must be
  re-run on the reporting hardware named in docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md. Determined
  vectors (the BSV block Merkle vector and the study CI-point JSON) are
  byte-stable and regenerated by `npm run reproduce`.
